# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Enquiry form delivery
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The quotation and contact forms POST to /api/enquiry, which sends the
# enquiry by email. Configure ONE of the two transports below.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local for development, and set the same variables in
# your hosting provider's dashboard for production. Never commit .env.local.
#
# With neither transport configured the form returns an honest error telling
# the visitor to email the company directly, and logs the enquiry to the
# server console — it never shows a false "sent" message.

# --- Option 1: any SMTP provider (recommended for production) --------------
# Works with Zoho, Google Workspace, Microsoft 365, Amazon SES, Postmark, etc.
# Using a mailbox on your own domain improves deliverability.
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.zoho.in
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_SECURE=false          # true for port 465
# SMTP_USER=website@sheetalaromatics.com
# SMTP_PASS=

# --- Option 2: Gmail with an App Password ----------------------------------
# Requires 2-Step Verification on the account, then an App Password generated
# at https://myaccount.google.com/apppasswords. A normal Gmail password will
# not work.
# GMAIL_USER=sheetalaromatics@gmail.com
# GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=

# --- Optional overrides -----------------------------------------------------
# Where enquiries are delivered. Defaults to the address in lib/site-config.ts.
# CONTACT_TO=sheetalaromatics@gmail.com
# The From address on outgoing notifications. Defaults to the SMTP/Gmail user.
# CONTACT_FROM=website@sheetalaromatics.com
